---
import Page from "@layouts/Page.astro";
import Section from "@components/Section.astro";
import SectionHead from "@components/SectionHead.astro";
import SectionSub from "@components/SectionSub.astro";
const title = "United Nations Joint Staff Pension Fund (UNJSPF)";
const subtitle = "Modernizing a Mission-Critical Platform for a Global Audience";
---

<Page title={title} subtitle={subtitle}>
  <Section>
    <SectionHead title="Summary" />
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto typography gap-4 flex flex-col flex-nowrap">
      <div class="text-pretty">
        <p>The <a href="https://unjspf.org/" target="_blank">United Nations Joint Staff Pension Fund</a> supports current and retired United Nations employees around the world. The organization’s website plays a critical role in communicating complex pension information to a diverse, international audience — many of whom rely on clarity, accessibility, and trust when navigating retirement-related content.</p>
        <p>I partnered with UNJSPF leadership, internal development teams, and UI/UX specialists to modernize an aging website, focusing on implementation, accessibility, and long-term maintainability while preserving stability for a mission-critical system.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>
  <Section>
    <SectionHead title="Project Snapshot" />
    <SectionSub>
      <div class="text-pretty flex flex-col gap-8">
        <div>
          <h3>Role</h3>
          <p class="mt-0">Human Factors Software Engineer / Front-End Implementation Lead</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Collaboration</h3>
          <p class="mt-0">
            UI/UX specialists (research, content strategy, interface design)
            <br />UNJSPF leadership and internal development team
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Scope</h3>
          <p class="mt-0">Front-end development, WordPress architecture, accessibility, editorial workflows</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Audience</h3>
          <p class="mt-0">Active and retired UN staff across multiple countries, languages, and accessibility needs</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Primary Goals</h3>
          <ul class="formatted">
            <li>Support a new content strategy with a clear, scalable site structure</li>
            <li>Improve accessibility and usability for a global audience</li>
            <li>Reduce reliance on developers for routine content updates</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </SectionSub>
  </Section>
  <Section>
    <SectionHead title="The Challenge" />
    <SectionSub>
      <div class="text-pretty">
        <p>Over time, the UNJSPF website had grown organically, resulting in fragmented content, inconsistent navigation, and publishing workflows that made even small updates dependent on developers.</p>
        <p>For an organization responsible for pension and retirement benefits, these issues introduced real risks — not only to usability and accessibility, but also to user confidence and internal efficiency. Any solution needed to modernize the platform while remaining stable, secure, and easy to maintain long-term.</p>
      </div>
    </SectionSub>
  </Section>
  <Section>
    <SectionHead title="My Role" />
    <SectionSub>
      <div class="text-pretty">
        <p>This project was highly collaborative.</p>
        <p>UI/UX specialists led user interviews, content strategy, and interface redesign. My role focused on translating that work into a reliable, accessible, and maintainable WordPress implementation that aligned with both user needs and internal workflows.</p>
        <p>I served as the bridge between strategy and execution — ensuring research insights and design decisions could be realistically supported by the site’s technical architecture without increasing complexity or technical debt.</p>
      </div>
    </SectionSub>
  </Section>
  <Section>
    <SectionHead title="Approach & Contributions" />
    <SectionSub>
      <div class="text-pretty flex flex-col gap-8">
        <div>
          <h3>Partnering During Research</h3>
          <ul class="formatted">
            <li>Collaborated with UI/UX specialists during user interviews with current and retired UN employees worldwide</li>
            <li>Helped evaluate research insights through a technical and accessibility lens to inform implementation decisions early</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Technical & Structural Analysis</h3>
          <ul class="formatted">
            <li>Conducted a comprehensive analysis of the existing website’s structure, templates, and publishing workflows</li>
            <li>Identified constraints and opportunities to support the new content strategy within WordPress</li>
            <li>Worked directly with content editors to understand workflow pain points and reduce friction</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Implementation Strategy</h3>
          <ul class="formatted">
            <li>Defined a WordPress architecture that supported the redesigned content hierarchy and navigation</li>
            <li>Prioritized accessibility, semantic structure, and consistency across templates</li>
            <li>Focused on flexibility for editors, minimizing the need for developer involvement in day-to-day updates</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </SectionSub>
  </Section>
  <Section>
    <SectionHead title="The Solution" />
    <SectionSub>
      <div class="text-pretty">
        <p>Working alongside UI/UX specialists and UN developers, I led the front-end implementation of a new WordPress platform that translated the redesigned experience into a stable, scalable system.</p>
        <p class="">The solution:</p>
        <ul class="formatted">
          <li>Supported the new content organization and interface design</li>
          <li>Improved accessibility and clarity for complex pension-related content</li>
          <li>Enabled non-technical staff to create, update, and manage content independently</li>
          <li>Reduced long-term maintenance overhead for the development team</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </SectionSub>
  </Section>
  <Section>
    <SectionHead title="Outcomes" />
    <SectionSub>
      <div class="text-pretty">
        <p class="">While the project emphasized long-term stability over short-term metrics, the redesigned platform delivered meaningful organizational improvements:</p>
        <ul class="formatted">
          <li>Clearer content structure for a diverse, global audience</li>
          <li>Improved confidence among content editors and stakeholders</li>
          <li>A maintainable foundation that supports future growth and accessibility improvements</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </SectionSub>
  </Section>
  <Section>
    <SectionHead title="Why This Project Matters" />
    <SectionSub>
      <p>This work reflects the type of role I’m most effective in: partnering with specialists, understanding user and organizational needs, and delivering thoughtful implementations that turn strategy into systems teams can actually maintain.</p>
      <p>Rather than focusing on visual design, I bring structure, accessibility, and execution rigor to complex projects — helping organizations modernize without introducing unnecessary risk.</p>
    </SectionSub>
  </Section>
</Page>
